From 216ccc9916b8a44a632aaebf70c0c98eada103b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:56:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Agent host: anchor branch changes on the session baseline
 checkpoint

Branch Changes are diffed against the merge-base with the base branch,
which assumes a session owns its branch. A session started on a
long-lived shared branch therefore reports that branch's entire
divergence: every session in the repository shows the same number, it
grows with each commit whether or not any session touched it, and a
session that edited two files can read as sixteen thousand insertions.

Anchor the diff on the session's baseline checkpoint when one exists.
That checkpoint is captured once per session per repository, so the
diff becomes the session's own footprint. A session that does own its
branch is unaffected, since its baseline is the branch point. Without a
baseline (no checkpoints, non-git folder, capture failed) the base
branch is still used.

The anchor is resolved in one place and used by both the primary and
per-repository diffs, so the branch changeset, the session-list chip
and every path that derives the chip from that changeset agree. Commit
and pull-request flows are untouched: they call the git service
directly with the base branch.
